    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the attacker has to make a new table for every single user just because of the salt, that sounds like a massive headache for them lol. is there any other way they'd try to crack it if they can't use rainbow tables? like do they just try to brute force it instead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Without rainbow tables, attackers typically resort to brute-force or dictionary attacks against the salted hash. Brute-forcing involves systematically trying every possible character combination until the computed hash matches the stored hash. Dictionary attacks use lists of common words and phrases. The salt forces these attacks to be done individually for each user, significantly slowing down the cracking process for the attacker.",
